{
  "_id": "fhSubBogwitch001",
  "name": "Bogwitch's Prank",
  "type": "consumable",
  "img": "icons/svg/item-bag.svg",
  "folder": "fhSubFantasy0001",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A small purple-capped fungus that grows on rotting logs in marshlands, visually identical to a popular edible variety. Foragers learn to tell the difference; their friends usually don't. Eaten unwittingly more often than not. Colors turn loud and faintly synesthetic, which makes for a dazzling performance and unreliable eyes.</p><p><strong><em>Desired effects on use.</em></strong> For 1 hour you have advantage on Charisma (Performance) checks and disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks.</p><p><strong><em>On use, save against addiction.</em></strong> Make a DC 12 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, you gain the Addicted condition from Bogwitch's Prank (see below).</p><p><strong><em>Addicted from Bogwitch's Prank.</em></strong> While you have this Addicted condition, you are also Poisoned and have disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks.</p><p><strong><em>Withdrawal.</em></strong> At the end of each Long Rest while addicted, you either take another dose or abstain. If you abstain, make a DC 11 Wisdom check to resist the craving; on a failure, you give in and take a dose. On a success, you go into withdrawal for 4 days, or half that if you succeed on a DC 12 Constitution saving throw. If you have no doses left, skip the Wisdom check. While in withdrawal you have disadvantage on Wisdom and Intelligence saving throws, and in combat you take 1d4 psychic damage at the start of each of your turns. Abstaining then takes only the Wisdom check, and taking any dose ends the withdrawal but not the addiction. When the withdrawal ends, so does the addiction.</p><p><strong><em>Overdose.</em></strong> If you take a dose while still under its effects, or once your tolerance is at its limit, there is a 10% chance you overdose: you take 2d6 psychic damage and have the Incapacitated condition for 1 round.</p><p><strong><em>Dosing others.</em></strong> As an action, you can slip a dose into food or drink within 5 feet. A creature that consumes it is dosed.</p><p><em>Requires ready paraphernalia that applies to ingested substances, such as an Apothecary's Vial or the Tongue of the Oracle.</em></p>"
    },
